DOCX export filter
==================

This filter converts an ODT package to a WordprocessingML DOCX package. It
traverses the ODT content with OdtReader and OdfTextReader backends, writes the
document and style XML, collects package parts in DocxFile, and emits OPC
relationship parts and [Content_Types].xml when creating the final package.

The current exporter supports a limited subset of DOCX. It writes basic text,
tables (column widths, cell/table borders, cell background, vertical alignment,
horizontal and vertical merges), lists and numbered paragraphs (via
word/numbering.xml and w:numPr), tab stops and tab characters, explicit page
breaks, keep-with-next/keep-together controls, inline PNG, JPEG, GIF, BMP, and
TIFF images, comments, hyperlinks, explicit spaces and line breaks, and maps a
broad subset of paragraph and character formatting (fonts, sizes, bold, italic,
underline variants, strikethrough, small caps, caps, letter spacing, text
scaling, super/subscript, colors, character and paragraph background, paragraph
borders, alignment, indentation, spacing, and heading outline levels). Page
borders are written as w:pgBorders, and ODF page background images are exported
as behind-text images in the section header so Word and LibreOffice display them
as watermarks. The first
paragraph's selected master page (or the first master page when none
is selected) is exported from styles.xml as word/header1.xml and
word/footer1.xml (including their images and tables), and the matching w:sectPr
with page size, margins, and header/footer references is appended to the
document body. Floating and inline placement, basic square/top-and-bottom/
run-through wrapping, tight/through contour wrapping, and image rotation are preserved. Image cropping,
SVG images, and many other advanced Word
features are not yet preserved; only the first master page is used and its
first/left header and footer variants are skipped. Unsupported ODF constructs
may be lost in conversion.

Key classes
-----------

DocxExport                  Coordinates ODT traversal, header/footer export,
                            and DOCX package output
OdfReaderDocxContext        Holds output XML writers, the current output part,
                            the section properties, and the package collector
OdfTextReaderDocxBackend    Converts ODF paragraphs, runs, links, and comments
DocxDrawReaderBackend       Embeds raster images and charts, with DrawingML placement
DocxChartWriter             Exports chart series and embedded editable XLSX data
DocxStyleWriter             Writes Word style definitions
DocxStyleHelper             Maps supported ODF text and paragraph properties
DocxNumbering               Maps ODF list styles to word/numbering.xml
DocxFile                    Collects package parts and writes the DOCX package
OpcRelSet                   Stores and serializes relationships for one part
OpcRelSetManager            Writes package-level and part-level relationships

Relationship sets are generated from the relationships registered during the
conversion. Add relationships through DocxFile::addRelationship so that the
relationship identifiers used in document XML match the emitted .rels parts.

Charts
------
Embedded ODF charts with local table data are exported as native DrawingML chart
parts with cached series, category labels, titles, and an embedded XLSX worksheet.
Bar, line, area, pie, ring, scatter, bubble, radar and stock charts are supported.
Area series order and bubble size/domain mappings follow the differing ODF and
DrawingML conventions. Advanced formatting (including 3D effects, secondary axes,
custom labels and exact legend/plot geometry) is not fully mapped yet. Linked
charts without local data, mixed chart types and unrecognized embedded objects
cause export to fail rather than produce a successful file missing the object.
Run tests/charts.py with calligraconverter and the local plugin environment for
chart/data round trips, workbook references, placement and unsupported-chart checks.

Office preset shapes
--------------------
The Words Shapes gallery exposes the native Office preset catalog. Preset
identity is stored as draw:type="ooxml-..." on enhanced geometry. DOCX export
writes editable WordprocessingShape objects, with size, placement, basic fill
and outline colors, mirroring, rotation and plain text. Import reconstructs
native enhanced geometry and retains preset identity for subsequent saves.
Arbitrary custom paths, adjustment handles, connector attachment semantics and
rich shape-text formatting are not fully mapped by this preset conversion.
Run tests/preset_shapes.py to check all 187 presets, Unicode text and repeated
save/open cycles. Native previews and saved geometry share the existing OOXML
preset definitions; sequentially reassigned guide names are normalized to avoid
recursive ODF equations (notably in the gear presets).

Formatting and run-structure regressions
---------------------------------------
Document-wide run defaults are written in w:docDefaults/w:rPrDefault. ODF
font-face identifiers are resolved to actual family names, including separate
Latin, Asian and complex-script fonts, sizes and language tags. The exporter
preserves double/colored underlines, hidden text, numeric super/subscript and
baseline resets, and explicit resets of capitalization, character spacing,
text scaling and paragraph keep controls. ODF automatic soft-page-break hints
are ignored instead of becoming forced Word page breaks.

Nested ODF spans are tracked as formatting scopes. Text, spaces, tabs and
fields emit flat Word runs; hyperlinks inside formatted spans remain real
hyperlinks. Footnote formatting scopes are isolated from the enclosing body
span. This avoids nested w:r elements and text/link loss when Word-compatible
applications reopen the package.

Run the common-ODT comparison fixture with the local installed native filter:

    /usr/bin/python3 filters/words/docx/export/tests/export_options.py \
      --output build/docx-export-options-new

Its 31 checks cover defaults, script-specific formatting, explicit resets,
run structure, nested hyperlink/note text, and reopened-PDF rendering. Boolean
and color values are compared semantically. The rendering check requires equal
page counts and at least 0.95 pixel similarity on each fixture page; it does
not certify exact visual identity or unsupported features.

To isolate export differences on an existing ODT:

    /usr/bin/python3 devtools/office/compare_docx_export.py input.odt \
      --baseline older-native.docx --output build/docx-export-comparison-new

The optional baseline must be an older export of the same input. Both native
and reference DOCX are independently reopened by LibreOffice for rendering.
Content, tables, notes, header/footer text, hyperlinks, image counts, page
counts, package integrity, source SHA-256 and per-page differences are recorded.
The existing page_margins.py, charts.py, primitive_shapes.py and preset_shapes.py
regressions can be run with the calligraconverter path and its plugin environment.
